            <div class="story-grid">
                <div>
                    <p class="section-subheading">Our Story</p>
                    <h2 class="section-heading">How We Came Together</h2>
                    <div class="section-divider"></div>
                    <p>Lock-in' Ringers didn't form by chance — they were brought together through a shared community. Each member found their way to barbershop through the Cloverdale Chordsmen, a barbershop chorus in the Lower Mainland of British Columbia, and through "Young Singers in Harmony," a program designed to introduce young people to the art form.</p>
                    <p>In 2024, the Chordsmen's musical director encouraged his youngest members to form a quartet and compete together. Joey, Sean, Steven, and Alex stepped up — and Lock-in' Ringers was born.</p>
                    <p>The lineup has shifted since then. In September 2026, Sean left the quartet and Kyler Hoffman — a member of the Cloverdale Chordsmen since 2025 — joined to anchor the chord on bass, with Alex moving to lead and Steven to baritone.</p>
                    <p>The name is a nod to one of barbershop's most iconic moments: when four voices "lock in" together and the chord rings with a resonance greater than any one singer. That's the sound they're chasing every time they step on stage.</p>
                </div>
