                <article class="member-card">
                    <div class="member-photo"><img src="/resources/img/members/joey.jpg" alt="Joey Driedger"></div>
                    <div class="member-info">
                        <p class="member-part">Tenor</p>
                        <h2 class="member-name">Joey Driedger</h2>
                        <p class="member-bio">A jazz band trip to Idaho was all it took — when chorus director Keith Richmond introduced Joey to barbershop harmony, he was hooked. Back home, band teacher invited him to join the Cloverdale Chordsmen, where the Young Singers in Harmony program eventually brought him together with Steven, Alex, and the quartet's original lead, Sean Hylands. Outside of music, Joey is a BCIT Games Development student whose work can be found at <a href="https://joeydriedger.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">joeydriedger.ca</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="member-card">
                    <div class="member-photo"><img src="/resources/img/members/alex.jpg" alt="Alex Kerry"></div>
                    <div class="member-info">
                        <p class="member-part">Lead</p>
                        <h2 class="member-name">Alex Kerry</h2>
                        <p class="member-bio">Alex’s love of music began in middle and high school, where he performed in bands, choirs, vocal jazz, and musical theatre. In 2023, he joined Keith Richmond’s Cloverdale Chordsmen, singing baritone before forming a quartet with the guys a year later. Outside of barbershop, Alex is a full-time SFU undergraduate studying Archaeology, Anthropology, Geography, and Religion, while also pursuing various “side quests” in bartending, marketing, telecommunications, and Vancouver’s film industry.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="member-card">
                    <div class="member-photo"><img src="/resources/img/members/steven.jpg" alt="Steven Rutherford"></div>
                    <div class="member-info">
                        <p class="member-part">Baritone</p>
                        <h2 class="member-name">Steven Rutherford</h2>
                        <p class="member-bio">Steven’s high school music director, Patti Thorpe, introduced him to barbershop music through the 2019 Young Singers in Harmony program. There, he met Keith Richmond, who eventually invited Steven to join the Cloverdale Chordsmen in 2023. As of right now, Steven currently serves as the music teacher for drums and percussion at Long and McQuade.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="member-card">
